# Rotate Secrets

Procedure for rotating secrets in Key Vault and updating downstream consumers for `<%workload%>`.

<!-- TODO: Fill in project-specific secret names and Key Vault details after scaffolding. -->

## Prereqs

- Access: `Key Vault Secrets Officer` role on `kv-<%workload%>-<env>`, or equivalent.
- State: Know which secret is being rotated and its consumers (Container Apps, Function Apps, pipelines).
- Tools: `az` CLI authenticated (`az login`), `gh` CLI authenticated.

## Steps

### 1. Generate the new secret value

Generate a new credential at the secret's source (e.g. storage account key, API key portal, `openssl rand -base64 32` for symmetric keys).

```bash
# Example: rotate a storage account key
az storage account keys renew \
  --account-name st<%workload%><env> \
  --resource-group rg-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --key primary
NEW_VALUE=$(az storage account keys list \
  --account-name st<%workload%><env> \
  --resource-group rg-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --query "[0].value" -o tsv)
```

### 2. Update the secret in Key Vault

```bash
az keyvault secret set \
  --vault-name kv-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --name <SECRET_NAME> \
  --value "$NEW_VALUE"
```

### 3. Force a new revision (Container Apps)

Key Vault references in Container Apps resolve at revision creation — a running revision will not pick up the new secret without a new revision.

```bash
az containerapp update \
  --name ca-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --resource-group rg-<%workload%>-<env>
```

<!-- TODO: List all Container Apps that consume this secret. -->

### 4. Restart consuming Function Apps (if applicable)

```bash
az functionapp restart \
  --name func-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --resource-group rg-<%workload%>-<env>
```

<!-- TODO: List all Function Apps that consume this secret. -->

### 5. Update local `.env.local` (developer machines)

Notify all developers to update their local `.env.local` with the new value. Distribute via password manager or 1Password CLI — never via Slack/email.

### 6. Revoke the old secret value

If the secret is a key with a secondary (e.g. storage account), disable or delete the old primary after confirming consumers have picked up the new value.

## Verify

- [ ] New revision of Container App is `Running`.
- [ ] Function App responds to health check.
- [ ] No `403` / `KeyVault` errors in Application Insights.
- [ ] Old secret value is revoked / disabled at its source.

## Rollback

If the new secret causes errors:

1. Re-set the previous value in Key Vault (`az keyvault secret set --value "<OLD_VALUE>"`).
2. Force a new Container App revision.
3. Restart Function Apps.

## Known failure modes

- **Container App still using old secret**: check that a new revision was created and is receiving traffic. `az containerapp revision list` to confirm.
- **KV reference resolution delay**: new revision can take 1-2 minutes to pull from KV. Wait and re-check.
- **`AADSTS` on OIDC login**: unrelated — check federated credential subjects in `secrets.md`.

